  "details": "I want to have a specific movement for just the avatar's arms from ExMenu.\n\nI have set up animation for just the arms in the Action Layer, and set Left Hand/Right Hand to Animation using Tracking Control.\n\nDespite this, the Shoulder bone sometimes follows the controller movement.\n\nSpecifically, when I place the controller between around my ear and behind the face, only the Shoulder bone follows it a little.\n\nThe other bones, UpperArms, LowerArms and Hands, are properly Animation-dominated.\n\nSometimes it works as expected, and whether it succeeds or not depends on the contents of the Animation Clip, I think.\n\nI don't understand the difference between why it works in some cases and not in others.\n\nI have uploaded the reproduction assets as a unitypackage here.\n\nhttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1SRkRNxqTKdyhx3xEMglRMXxfvCI_T5R8/view?usp=sharing\n\nThe sample avatar has been modified, so build it, log in as VR, and check Pattern 1 and 2 in ExMenu.\n\nPattern 1 works as expected. The shoulders completely ignore the controller movement.\n\nPattern 2 is strange. When the controller is between the ear and behind the face, the shoulders are pulled and move.\n\nThe same issue occurs when I switch the Animation Clips of the two Patterns, so it shouldn’t be a problem with the Animator Controller.\n\nTest Avatar ID: \n\navtr_8afd8f11-ca3e-4bb7-8c54-1c7291e9ff8b\n\nTest World for reproduction video:\n\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_01025423-c339-4735-8af9-ba45cc9e46f2/info",
